// Rep Max questions: Mathematics (Pearson Edexcel 1MA1), GCSE. One question per line, no commas between lines.
// Fields: id (unique), s (subject), t (topic id from spec.json), lv (1 warm-up, 2 working set, 3 hardest; Higher-only topics are 3),
// q (question; maths between $ signs, backslashes doubled), code (optional), o (four options), a (index 0-3 of the right one), x (explanation).
// Written by AI (Sonnet) and checked independently by AI (Opus), 15 Nov 2026; logs in provenance/ted-gcse/questions/.
{"id":"gma-001","s":"maths","t":"N1-N3","lv":1,"q":"Work out $3 + 4 \\times 2^2 - 5$.","o":["$23$","$14$","$62$","$116$"],"a":1,"x":"Powers first: $2^2=4$. Then multiply: $4\\times4=16$. Then $3+16-5=14$."}
{"id":"gma-002","s":"maths","t":"N1-N3","lv":2,"q":"Work out $2\\frac{1}{3} + 1\\frac{3}{4}$.","o":["$4\\frac{4}{7}$","$3\\frac{1}{12}$","$4\\frac{1}{7}$","$4\\frac{1}{12}$"],"a":3,"x":"Add whole numbers: 3. Then $\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{4}{12}+\\frac{9}{12}=\\frac{13}{12}=1\\frac{1}{12}$. Total $4\\frac{1}{12}$."}
{"id":"gma-003","s":"maths","t":"N4-N5","lv":1,"q":"What is the highest common factor (HCF) of 24 and 36?","o":["$6$","$72$","$4$","$12$"],"a":3,"x":"Factors of 24 and 36 shared: 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 12. The highest is 12. (72 is the LCM.)"}
{"id":"gma-004","s":"maths","t":"N6-N7","lv":1,"q":"Work out the value of $2^3 \\times 2^4$.","o":["$4096$","$56$","$128$","$14$"],"a":2,"x":"Add the powers when multiplying: $2^3\\times2^4=2^7=128$."}
{"id":"gma-005","s":"maths","t":"N8","lv":1,"q":"A circle has radius 3 cm. What is its area, in terms of $\\pi$?","o":["$9\\pi$ cm²","$6\\pi$ cm²","$18\\pi$ cm²","$3\\pi$ cm²"],"a":0,"x":"Area $=\\pi r^2=\\pi\\times3^2=9\\pi$. ($6\\pi$ is the circumference.)"}
{"id":"gma-006","s":"maths","t":"N9","lv":1,"q":"Write $0.00045$ in standard form.","o":["$4.5\\times10^{-3}$","$45\\times10^{-5}$","$4.5\\times10^{4}$","$4.5\\times10^{-4}$"],"a":3,"x":"Move the decimal point 4 places right to get $4.5$, so the power is $-4$. ($45\\times10^{-5}$ is not standard form.)"}
{"id":"gma-007","s":"maths","t":"N10-N12","lv":1,"q":"Write $0.375$ as a fraction in its simplest form.","o":["$\\frac{3}{8}$","$\\frac{3}{10}$","$\\frac{5}{8}$","$\\frac{37}{100}$"],"a":0,"x":"$0.375=\\frac{375}{1000}$. Divide top and bottom by 125 to get $\\frac{3}{8}$."}
{"id":"gma-008","s":"maths","t":"N13-N16","lv":2,"q":"A number $x$ is rounded to 1 decimal place. The result is $7.4$. What is the error interval for $x$?","o":["$7.35 \\le x \\le 7.45$","$7.4 \\le x < 7.5$","$7.3 \\le x < 7.5$","$7.35 \\le x < 7.45$"],"a":3,"x":"Half a unit of the last place is $0.05$. So $7.35$ up to but not including $7.45$, since $7.45$ rounds up to $7.5$."}
{"id":"gma-009","s":"maths","t":"A1-A3","lv":1,"q":"Work out the value of $2x^2 - x$ when $x = -3$.","o":["$-15$","$39$","$21$","$-21$"],"a":2,"x":"Square first: $(-3)^2=9$, so $2\\times9=18$. Then $18-(-3)=21$."}
{"id":"gma-010","s":"maths","t":"A4","lv":1,"q":"Expand and simplify $(x+3)(x-5)$.","o":["$x^2+2x-15$","$x^2-2x+15$","$x^2-2x-15$","$x^2-8x-15$"],"a":2,"x":"$x^2-5x+3x-15=x^2-2x-15$."}
{"id":"gma-011","s":"maths","t":"A4","lv":2,"q":"Factorise $x^2-5x-14$.","o":["$(x-7)(x+2)$","$(x+7)(x-2)$","$(x-7)(x-2)$","$(x+7)(x+2)$"],"a":0,"x":"Find two numbers with product $-14$ and sum $-5$: $-7$ and $+2$."}
{"id":"gma-012","s":"maths","t":"A5","lv":2,"q":"Make $x$ the subject of $y=\\frac{x+4}{3}$.","o":["$x=3y-4$","$x=3y+4$","$x=\\frac{y}{3}-4$","$x=\\frac{y-4}{3}$"],"a":0,"x":"Multiply both sides by 3: $3y=x+4$. Then subtract 4: $x=3y-4$."}
{"id":"gma-013","s":"maths","t":"A6-A7","lv":1,"q":"Which of these is an identity (true for every value of $x$)?","o":["$(x+3)^2=x^2+9$","$2x+1=x+4$","$3(x+2)=3x+6$","$x^2=4x$"],"a":2,"x":"Expanding $3(x+2)$ gives $3x+6$ for every $x$, so we can write $3(x+2)\\equiv3x+6$. $(x+3)^2=x^2+6x+9$, and the other two are true only for some values of $x$."}
{"id":"gma-014","s":"maths","t":"A8-A10","lv":2,"q":"A line is parallel to $y=2x+5$ and passes through $(1, 3)$. What is its equation?","o":["$y=2x+1$","$y=2x+3$","$y=-2x+5$","$y=2x-1$"],"a":0,"x":"Parallel lines have gradient 2. Use $(1,3)$: $3=2\\times1+c$, so $c=1$."}
{"id":"gma-015","s":"maths","t":"A11-A12","lv":2,"q":"Where does the graph of $y=x^2-6x+5$ cross the $x$-axis?","o":["$x=-1$ and $x=-5$","$x=1$ and $x=5$","$x=-1$ and $x=5$","$x=0$ and $x=6$"],"a":1,"x":"Put $y=0$: $x^2-6x+5=(x-1)(x-5)=0$, so $x=1$ or $x=5$."}
{"id":"gma-016","s":"maths","t":"A13","lv":3,"q":"The graph of $y=f(x)$ has a minimum point at $(2,-1)$. Where is the minimum of $y=f(x-1)+4$?","o":["$(1, 3)$","$(3, 3)$","$(3, -5)$","$(1, -5)$"],"a":1,"x":"$f(x-1)$ moves the graph 1 to the right: $x=3$. The $+4$ moves it up 4: $y=-1+4=3$."}
{"id":"gma-017","s":"maths","t":"A14-A15","lv":1,"q":"On a distance-time graph, a horizontal line shows that the object is:","o":["not moving","moving at a steady speed","speeding up","returning to the start"],"a":0,"x":"Distance is not changing as time passes, so the object is stationary."}
{"id":"gma-018","s":"maths","t":"A16","lv":3,"q":"The point $(3,4)$ is on the circle $x^2+y^2=25$. What is the equation of the tangent to the circle at this point?","o":["$4x+3y=25$","$3x+4y=25$","$3x-4y=-7$","$4x-3y=0$"],"a":1,"x":"Radius gradient is $\\frac{4}{3}$, so the tangent gradient is $-\\frac{3}{4}$. $y-4=-\\frac{3}{4}(x-3)$ gives $3x+4y=25$."}
{"id":"gma-019","s":"maths","t":"A17-A18","lv":1,"q":"Solve $3x+7=22$.","o":["$x=\\frac{29}{3}$","$x=15$","$x=5$","$x=-5$"],"a":2,"x":"Subtract 7: $3x=15$. Divide by 3: $x=5$."}
{"id":"gma-020","s":"maths","t":"A17-A18","lv":2,"q":"Solve $x^2-3x-10=0$.","o":["$x=5$ or $x=-2$","$x=-5$ or $x=2$","$x=10$ or $x=-1$","$x=5$ or $x=2$"],"a":0,"x":"$(x-5)(x+2)=0$, so $x=5$ or $x=-2$."}
{"id":"gma-021","s":"maths","t":"A19","lv":2,"q":"Solve $2x+y=11$ and $x-y=1$.","o":["$x=3,\\ y=4$","$x=4,\\ y=3$","$x=5,\\ y=1$","$x=6,\\ y=-1$"],"a":1,"x":"Add the equations: $3x=12$, so $x=4$. Then $4-y=1$ gives $y=3$."}
{"id":"gma-022","s":"maths","t":"A20","lv":3,"q":"$x_{n+1}=\\sqrt{x_n+5}$ and $x_0=1$. Use a calculator to work out $x_2$, to 2 decimal places.","o":["$2.45$","$2.78$","$6.57$","$2.73$"],"a":3,"x":"$x_1=\\sqrt{1+5}=2.449\\ldots$ Then $x_2=\\sqrt{2.449\\ldots+5}=2.729\\ldots\\approx2.73$."}
{"id":"gma-023","s":"maths","t":"A21-A22","lv":2,"q":"Solve $5-2x \\le 11$.","o":["$x \\le -3$","$x \\ge 3$","$x \\ge -3$","$x \\le 3$"],"a":2,"x":"Subtract 5: $-2x\\le6$. Dividing by a negative number flips the sign: $x\\ge-3$."}
{"id":"gma-024","s":"maths","t":"A23-A25","lv":1,"q":"Find the $n$th term of the sequence 5, 8, 11, 14, ...","o":["$3n+2$","$3n+5$","$5n+3$","$n+3$"],"a":0,"x":"The difference is 3, so start with $3n$. When $n=1$, $3n=3$; add 2 to get 5."}
{"id":"gma-025","s":"maths","t":"R1-R2","lv":2,"q":"On a map with scale 1 : 50 000, two towns are 4 cm apart. What is the real distance?","o":["20 km","2 km","200 m","0.2 km"],"a":1,"x":"$4\\times50\\,000=200\\,000$ cm. Divide by 100 for metres: 2000 m, which is 2 km."}
{"id":"gma-026","s":"maths","t":"R3-R8","lv":1,"q":"Write the ratio $18:24$ in its simplest form.","o":["$9:12$","$2:3$","$4:3$","$3:4$"],"a":3,"x":"Divide both numbers by their HCF, 6: $18\\div6=3$ and $24\\div6=4$."}
{"id":"gma-027","s":"maths","t":"R9","lv":2,"q":"After a 20% increase, a price is £90. What was the price before the increase?","o":["£72","£70","£108","£75"],"a":3,"x":"£90 is 120% of the original. Divide by 1.2: $90\\div1.2=75$."}
{"id":"gma-028","s":"maths","t":"R10-R11","lv":2,"q":"A metal block has mass 540 g and volume 200 cm³. What is its density?","o":["2.7 g/cm³","0.37 g/cm³","340 g/cm³","27 g/cm³"],"a":0,"x":"Density $=\\text{mass}\\div\\text{volume}=540\\div200=2.7$ g/cm³."}
{"id":"gma-029","s":"maths","t":"R12-R14","lv":3,"q":"Two similar solids have lengths in the ratio $2:5$. The smaller has volume 40 cm³. What is the volume of the larger?","o":["250 cm³","100 cm³","625 cm³","1000 cm³"],"a":2,"x":"Volume scale factor is the cube of the length factor: $(\\frac{5}{2})^3=15.625$. Then $40\\times15.625=625$."}
{"id":"gma-030","s":"maths","t":"R15","lv":3,"q":"A tangent is drawn at $t=3$ s on a distance-time graph. It passes through $(1, 2)$ and $(5, 14)$ (distance in m). What is the speed at $t=3$?","o":["$\\frac{1}{3}$ m/s","2.8 m/s","12 m/s","3 m/s"],"a":3,"x":"The speed is the gradient of the tangent: $\\frac{14-2}{5-1}=3$ m/s."}
{"id":"gma-031","s":"maths","t":"R16","lv":2,"q":"£2000 is invested at 4% compound interest per year. How much is it worth after 3 years?","o":["£2240.00","£2249.73","£2163.20","£2339.72"],"a":1,"x":"Multiply by 1.04 three times: $2000\\times1.04^3=2249.73$. (£2240 would be simple interest.)"}
{"id":"gma-032","s":"maths","t":"G1-G2","lv":1,"q":"Which locus is the set of points equidistant from two fixed points $A$ and $B$?","o":["The perpendicular bisector of $AB$","The bisector of an angle at $A$","A circle with centre $A$","A line parallel to $AB$"],"a":0,"x":"Points the same distance from $A$ and $B$ lie on the line that cuts $AB$ in half at right angles."}
{"id":"gma-033","s":"maths","t":"G3-G4","lv":1,"q":"What is the sum of the interior angles of a hexagon?","o":["$540^\\circ$","$1080^\\circ$","$720^\\circ$","$360^\\circ$"],"a":2,"x":"Sum $=(n-2)\\times180=4\\times180=720^\\circ$."}
{"id":"gma-034","s":"maths","t":"G3-G4","lv":2,"q":"Each exterior angle of a regular polygon is $18^\\circ$. How many sides does it have?","o":["$10$","$18$","$22$","$20$"],"a":3,"x":"Exterior angles add up to $360^\\circ$. $360\\div18=20$ sides."}
{"id":"gma-035","s":"maths","t":"G5-G6","lv":1,"q":"A right-angled triangle has shorter sides 6 cm and 8 cm. How long is the hypotenuse?","o":["14 cm","100 cm","10 cm","5.3 cm"],"a":2,"x":"$6^2+8^2=36+64=100$. The hypotenuse is $\\sqrt{100}=10$ cm."}
{"id":"gma-036","s":"maths","t":"G7-G8","lv":2,"q":"The point $(2,1)$ is rotated $90^\\circ$ anticlockwise about the origin. What are its new coordinates?","o":["$(1, -2)$","$(-2, -1)$","$(-1, 2)$","$(2, -1)$"],"a":2,"x":"A $90^\\circ$ anticlockwise turn takes $(x,y)$ to $(-y,x)$. So $(2,1)\\to(-1,2)$."}
{"id":"gma-037","s":"maths","t":"G9-G10","lv":3,"q":"$AB$ is a diameter of a circle and $C$ is a point on the circumference. Angle $CAB=34^\\circ$. What is angle $ABC$?","o":["$73^\\circ$","$34^\\circ$","$146^\\circ$","$56^\\circ$"],"a":3,"x":"Angle $ACB=90^\\circ$ (the angle in a semicircle is a right angle). Angles in a triangle add to $180^\\circ$, so angle $ABC=180-90-34=56^\\circ$."}
{"id":"gma-038","s":"maths","t":"G11-G15","lv":2,"q":"The bearing of $B$ from $A$ is $065^\\circ$. What is the bearing of $A$ from $B$?","o":["$115^\\circ$","$245^\\circ$","$025^\\circ$","$295^\\circ$"],"a":1,"x":"Back bearings differ by $180^\\circ$: $65+180=245^\\circ$."}
{"id":"gma-039","s":"maths","t":"G16-G18","lv":2,"q":"A sector has radius 6 cm and angle $60^\\circ$. What is its area, in terms of $\\pi$?","o":["$12\\pi$ cm²","$36\\pi$ cm²","$6\\pi$ cm²","$2\\pi$ cm²"],"a":2,"x":"Area $=\\frac{60}{360}\\times\\pi\\times6^2=\\frac{1}{6}\\times36\\pi=6\\pi$."}
{"id":"gma-040","s":"maths","t":"G16-G18","lv":2,"q":"A cone has base radius 6 cm and vertical height 8 cm. Curved surface area $=\\pi rl$, where $l$ is the slant height. What is its curved surface area, in terms of $\\pi$?","o":["$48\\pi$ cm²","$60\\pi$ cm²","$96\\pi$ cm²","$120\\pi$ cm²"],"a":1,"x":"Slant height $=\\sqrt{6^2+8^2}=10$. Curved area $=\\pi rl=\\pi\\times6\\times10=60\\pi$."}
{"id":"gma-041","s":"maths","t":"G19-G21","lv":2,"q":"In a right-angled triangle, angle $x$ has opposite side 6 cm and adjacent side 8 cm. Use a calculator to find $x$ to 1 decimal place.","o":["$36.9^\\circ$","$53.1^\\circ$","$48.6^\\circ$","$41.4^\\circ$"],"a":0,"x":"$\\tan x=\\frac{6}{8}$, so $x=\\tan^{-1}(0.75)=36.9^\\circ$."}
{"id":"gma-042","s":"maths","t":"G22-G23","lv":3,"q":"A triangle has sides 8 cm and 5 cm with an angle of $30^\\circ$ between them. What is its area?","o":["20 cm²","17.3 cm²","34.6 cm²","10 cm²"],"a":3,"x":"Area $=\\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin C=\\frac{1}{2}\\times8\\times5\\times\\sin30^\\circ=20\\times0.5=10$."}
{"id":"gma-043","s":"maths","t":"G24-G25","lv":2,"q":"$\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\-2\\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}$. Work out $2\\mathbf{a}-\\mathbf{b}$.","o":["$\\begin{pmatrix}7\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\-8\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\-10\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}$"],"a":1,"x":"$2\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{pmatrix}6\\\\-4\\end{pmatrix}$. Subtract $\\mathbf{b}$: $\\begin{pmatrix}6-1\\\\-4-4\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\-8\\end{pmatrix}$."}
{"id":"gma-044","s":"maths","t":"P1-P5","lv":1,"q":"The probability that a counter drawn from a bag is blue is 0.35. What is the probability that it is not blue?","o":["$0.35$","$0.45$","$0.7$","$0.65$"],"a":3,"x":"Probabilities of an event and its opposite add to 1. $1-0.35=0.65$."}
{"id":"gma-045","s":"maths","t":"P6-P8","lv":3,"q":"Bag $A$ gives a red counter with probability 0.3. Bag $B$ gives red with probability 0.4. One counter is taken from each bag. What is P(at least one red)?","o":["$0.12$","$0.46$","$0.58$","$0.7$"],"a":2,"x":"P(no red) $=0.7\\times0.6=0.42$. So P(at least one red) $=1-0.42=0.58$."}
{"id":"gma-046","s":"maths","t":"P9","lv":3,"q":"Of 20 boys, 14 play football. Of 20 girls, 9 play football. A football player is chosen at random. What is the probability they are a girl?","o":["$\\frac{9}{20}$","$\\frac{9}{40}$","$\\frac{9}{23}$","$\\frac{11}{23}$"],"a":2,"x":"Football players: $14+9=23$. Of these, 9 are girls, so the probability is $\\frac{9}{23}$."}
{"id":"gma-047","s":"maths","t":"S1-S2","lv":2,"q":"A school has 600 pupils, 180 of them in Year 10. A sample of 50 pupils is taken, with each year group in the same proportion as in the school. How many should be from Year 10?","o":["$15$","$18$","$30$","$10$"],"a":0,"x":"Year 10 is $\\frac{180}{600}=30\\%$ of the school. $30\\%$ of 50 is 15."}
{"id":"gma-048","s":"maths","t":"S3","lv":3,"q":"A histogram has a bar for $0 \\le t < 10$ of height 3 and a bar for $10 \\le t < 30$ of height 1.5. The vertical axis is frequency density. What is the total frequency of the two bars?","o":["$4.5$","$30$","$90$","$60$"],"a":3,"x":"Frequency $=$ frequency density $\\times$ class width. $3\\times10=30$ and $1.5\\times20=30$. Total $60$."}
{"id":"gma-049","s":"maths","t":"S4-S5","lv":2,"q":"The mean of five numbers is 8. A sixth number is added and the mean becomes 9. What is the sixth number?","o":["$9$","$14$","$10$","$17$"],"a":1,"x":"Total of five $=40$. Total of six $=54$. The new number is $54-40=14$."}
{"id":"gma-050","s":"maths","t":"S6","lv":1,"q":"As the temperature rises, sales of hot drinks fall. What type of correlation is this?","o":["Positive correlation","Negative correlation","No correlation","Perfect correlation"],"a":1,"x":"One quantity increases while the other decreases, so the correlation is negative."}
